  "question": {
    "text": "To a solution of a colourless efflorescent sodium salt, when dilute acid is added, a colourless gas is evolved along with formation of a white precipitate. Acidified dichromate solution turns green when the colourless gas is passed through it. The sodium salt is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{Na}_{2} \\mathrm{SO}_{3}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{Na}_{2} \\mathrm{~S}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{Na}_{2} \\mathrm{~S}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{3}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{Na}_{2} \\mathrm{~S}_{4} \\mathrm{O}_{6}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hint: \r\n$\\underset{\\text { (colouriess, efflorescent) }}{\\mathrm{Na}_{2} \\mathrm{~S}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{3}(\\mathrm{~s})}+2 \\mathrm{H}^{+}(\\mathrm{dil} .) \\rightarrow \\mathrm{S}(\\mathrm{s})+2 \\mathrm{Na}^{+}(\\mathrm{aq})+\\mathrm{SO}_{2} \\uparrow+\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}(\\ell)$\r\n$\\mathrm{K}_{2} \\mathrm{Cr}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{7}($ aq. $)+3 \\mathrm{SO}_{2}(\\mathrm{~g})+2 \\mathrm{H}^{+}(\\mathrm{aq} .) \\longrightarrow 2 \\mathrm{~K}^{+}($ aq. $)+\\underset{(\\text { green })}{2 \\mathrm{Cr}^{+3}}(\\mathrm{aq})+\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}(\\ell)+3 \\mathrm{SO}_{4}^{-2}(\\mathrm{aq})$"
  }
}